(6080184, 894772, 60495, '<td valign="top">I know animals never pose like we would like but to me this image suffers because backside is so prominent. I belong to a wildlife photo club and one thing they have taught me is that people hate to see the rear of any animal and even though the head is turned towards the camera the rear becomes to much of the focal point. It would also IMO be more appealing if the crop was not as centered and the weed was not cluttering up the side of the animal but again they never cooperate so some times you get what you can. I do like the way you captured the animal in a clearing and the corn stalks make a decent backdrop to the shot. Hope the info helps, good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I know animals never pose like we would like but to me this image suffers because backside is so prominent. I belong to a wildlife photo club and one thing they have taught me is that people hate to see the rear of any animal and even though the head is turned towards the camera the rear becomes to much of the focal point. It would also IMO be more appealing if the crop was not as centered and the weed was not cluttering up the side of the animal but again they never cooperate so some times you get what you can. I do like the way you captured the animal in a clearing and the corn stalks make a decent backdrop to the shot. Hope the info helps, good luck in the challenge.', '2010-07-04 22:15:08.000000', NULL, 1),
