(6082609, 888844, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A bizarre scene - a good thing! Grabs the viewer''s attention and makes us wonder what is going on here; what''s the story. I like the eclectic dress of the guy on the right and the general mania of the shot.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The technicals are a bit vanilla - large depth of field robs the characters of interest and the flash lighting is a bit flat.<br/> <br/>Overall: Interesting but not one I''d want on the wall.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A bizarre scene - a good thing! Grabs the viewer''s attention and makes us wonder what is going on here; what''s the story. I like the eclectic dress of the guy on the right and the general mania of the shot. Critical stuff: The technicals are a bit vanilla - large depth of field robs the characters of interest and the flash lighting is a bit flat. Overall: Interesting but not one I''d want on the wall.', '2010-07-06 18:51:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6082613, 894690, 86218, '<td valign="top">Beautifull</td>', 'Beautifull', '2010-07-06 18:53:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6082618, 893398, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Very nice street shot - interesting character with an interesting backdrop. The interplay between the owl and the girl works really well. I really like the arm in the window too. I''m normally not fond of centred compositions, but this works well.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - I think, subject-wise, there is only so much interest in this scene, nbut you have certainly made the most of what was there.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Very nice street shot - interesting character with an interesting backdrop. The interplay between the owl and the girl works really well. I really like the arm in the window too. I''m normally not fond of centred compositions, but this works well. Critical stuff: Not much - I think, subject-wise, there is only so much interest in this scene, nbut you have certainly made the most of what was there.', '2010-07-06 18:57:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6082623, 894807, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives:Very intriguing - a nice spot through the trees and your dark, grainy, contrasty approach to the edit suits the subject really well. I particularly like the head shine! The whole composition makes me wonder where you were in relation to the subject; always a good thing to leave the viewer guessing.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: More often than not, I''m not a fan of (very) landscape orientations. I don''t dislike this one but it hasn''t changed my mind.<br/> <br/>Overall: Nice juxtaposition of elements - very effective image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives:Very intriguing - a nice spot through the trees and your dark, grainy, contrasty approach to the edit suits the subject really well. I particularly like the head shine! The whole composition makes me wonder where you were in relation to the subject; always a good thing to leave the viewer guessing. Critical stuff: More often than not, I''m not a fan of (very) landscape orientations. I don''t dislike this one but it hasn''t changed my mind. Overall: Nice juxtaposition of elements - very effective image.', '2010-07-06 19:05:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6082628, 894767, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the way you have chosen to shoot this - the offset and rotation contributes things to the image which would have been lost with a straighter composition. Your colour handling is also effective, capturing an indoor feel. I also like the way that we can''t help but try to count the storeys (10??)<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much - there is a finite amount of interest in this scene, but I like what you''ve done with it.<br/> <br/>Overall: An effective image, made so by your composition choices.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like the way you have chosen to shoot this - the offset and rotation contributes things to the image which would have been lost with a straighter composition. Your colour handling is also effective, capturing an indoor feel. I also like the way that we can''t help but try to count the storeys (10??) Critical stuff: Not much - there is a finite amount of interest in this scene, but I like what you''ve done with it. Overall: An effective image, made so by your composition choices.', '2010-07-06 19:10:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6082635, 894742, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Great juxtaposition of elements, making the lantern appear moonlike. The architecture is interesting and there is enough story in the people to make them interesting subjects too.I like how you''ve handled / maintained the luminosity levels.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''ve never been a fan of the Topazzy type of editing - it always makes things look messy to my eye. The people are particularly afflicted.<br/> <br/>Overall: Great composition, but for me, a suboptimal edit.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Great juxtaposition of elements, making the lantern appear moonlike. The architecture is interesting and there is enough story in the people to make them interesting subjects too.I like how you''ve handled / maintained the luminosity levels. Critical stuff: I''ve never been a fan of the Topazzy type of editing - it always makes things look messy to my eye. The people are particularly afflicted. Overall: Great composition, but for me, a suboptimal edit.', '2010-07-06 19:14:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6082640, 890529, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Favourited this earlier, back to comment and vote. A clear 10 - no doubt. One of my favourite images I have ever seen on DPC. Masterful edit - such confidence to let areas blow, knowing how that would facilitated the anchoring of the eye to your subject. The high key, high contrast monochrome is inspired. The girl is delightful and looks so tiny compared to the hand. I suspect I have already favourited the photographer but I can''t wait to see who this is.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: If I said anything here I would deserve to be banned from DPC.<br/> <br/>Overall: Absolute top drawer stuff. I expect to see this on 1x too. Thanks for sharing this.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Favourited this earlier, back to comment and vote. A clear 10 - no doubt. One of my favourite images I have ever seen on DPC. Masterful edit - such confidence to let areas blow, knowing how that would facilitated the anchoring of the eye to your subject. The high key, high contrast monochrome is inspired. The girl is delightful and looks so tiny compared to the hand. I suspect I have already favourited the photographer but I can''t wait to see who this is. Critical stuff: If I said anything here I would deserve to be banned from DPC. Overall: Absolute top drawer stuff. I expect to see this on 1x too. Thanks for sharing this.', '2010-07-06 19:20:38.000000', NULL, 1),
