(6086317, 894773, 17507, '<td valign="top">Wow, a 5.42? This was one of a handful of 8s that I gave. Although the processing was a bit rough and the sharpening could have stood to be reworked, it''s a strong image with a lot of solemnity, and the ruined pier is not the sort of thing you see every day. Really very nicely done.</td>', 'Wow, a 5.42? This was one of a handful of 8s that I gave. Although the processing was a bit rough and the sharpening could have stood to be reworked, it''s a strong image with a lot of solemnity, and the ruined pier is not the sort of thing you see every day. Really very nicely done.', '2010-07-09 10:02:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6086318, 893366, 17507, '<td valign="top">I didn''t drag your average down, but my 6 didn''t help you a whole lot, either. I think I may simply be a poor student of aerial photography. What most caught my eye was the wheels folded up against the fuselage--I don''t think I''ve seen that before, and certainly not from this angle.<br/> <br/>And it''s quite true--broad appeal can be pretty hard to predict.</td>', 'I didn''t drag your average down, but my 6 didn''t help you a whole lot, either. I think I may simply be a poor student of aerial photography. What most caught my eye was the wheels folded up against the fuselage--I don''t think I''ve seen that before, and certainly not from this angle. And it''s quite true--broad appeal can be pretty hard to predict.', '2010-07-09 10:04:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(6086320, 894339, 9114, '<td valign="top">Anne Geddes move over, Erin has arrived!<br/>Wonderful!<br/>Is there a link to making the crafty hat you would share?<br/>Debbi<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-07-09 09:12:32.</i></td>', 'Anne Geddes move over, Erin has arrived!Wonderful!Is there a link to making the crafty hat you would share?Debbi', '2010-07-09 10:07:21.000000', '2010-07-09 10:12:32.000000', 0),
